# Claim Entity & Lifecycle

Spec: ClaimLifecycle
Purpose:
  Define the claim entity system — knowledge assertions that carry
  evidence, confidence, and a lifecycle. Claims sit between raw
  observations and validated knowledge, providing an auditable layer
  where AI states "we believe X" before X becomes project rule.

Owns: lifecycle/claims.sdd

## Claim Lifecycle

  PROPOSED
    ↓
  SUPPORTED
    ↓
  VALIDATED
    ↓
  ACTIVE
    ↓
  CHALLENGED
    ↓
  INVALIDATED | SUPERSEDED

  PROPOSED:
    description: Initial claim submitted by AI with supporting evidence
    confidence_required: LOW
    action: visible in claim registry, no authoritative weight

  SUPPORTED:
    description: Claim has supporting evidence from 2+ independent sources
    confidence_required: MEDIUM
    action: may be referenced in task context with qualification

  VALIDATED:
    description: Claim confirmed by passing tests or human review
    confidence_required: HIGH
    action: included in standard context compilation

  ACTIVE:
    description: Claim is in active use across the project
    confidence_required: HIGH
    action: default reference target, included in all relevant context

  CHALLENGED:
    description: A @challenge.* has been filed against this claim
    confidence: downgraded to MEDIUM
    action: flagged for review, excluded from new task context

  INVALIDATED:
    description: Challenge accepted — claim is false or outdated
    confidence: LOW
    action: removed from context compilation, retained for history

  SUPERSEDED:
    description: Replaced by a newer @claim.* entity
    confidence: depends on new claim
    action: redirect references to successor claim

## Claim Evidence Types

  code:        observed in source files
  tests:       covered by passing tests
  tasks:       applied in a completed task
  decisions:   referenced by a human-approved decision
  production:  deployed and running in production
  external:    cited from external source (paper, repo, doc)
  human:       explicitly reviewed or approved by a human
  observation: raw @observation.* entry

## Promotion Rules

  [CLAIM-01] A claim in PROPOSED state MUST NOT be used as authoritative
             in any task context.

  [CLAIM-02] Promotion from PROPOSED to SUPPORTED requires at least 2
             independent evidence sources.

  [CLAIM-03] Promotion from SUPPORTED to VALIDATED requires either
             passing tests OR human review.

  [CLAIM-04] Promotion from VALIDATED to ACTIVE requires usage in at
             least 1 completed task OR production deployment.

  [CLAIM-05] Claims with trust score < 0.5 MUST include a
             confidence: LOW qualifier when referenced.

  [CLAIM-06] AI CANNOT promote its own claims to VALIDATED without
             human approval.

  [CLAIM-07] Claims that are challenged MUST be reviewed within 7 days
             by a human or automated gate.

  [CLAIM-08] Superseded claims MUST retain their evidence and a
             superseded_by pointer to the successor claim.

## Claim Format

  @claim.C11

  statement:
      Payment retries must be idempotent

  confidence:
    level: HIGH
    score: 0.91

  supported_by:
    - @evidence.E31
    - @decision.D88
    - @code.payment.retry.go

  challenged_by:
    []  (empty when not challenged)

  status:
    VALIDATED

  domain:
    payment

  scope:
    global

  origin:
    @discovery.D44

  provenance:
      discovered_from: @tmp.payment-service
    source: payment-service repository
    extracted_by: AI
    validated_by: @task.1044
    validated_at: 2026-08-31

  generation:
    1

## Confidence Propagation

  When a claim is used to support a skill, concept, or decision, its
  confidence propagates as a lower bound:

  - HIGH claim → supported knowledge confidence floor: 0.7
  - MEDIUM claim → supported knowledge confidence floor: 0.4
  - LOW claim → supported knowledge confidence floor: 0.0 (must qualify)

  [PROP-01] AI MUST state claim confidence when referencing a claim.
  [PROP-02] Knowledge supported only by LOW-confidence claims MUST
            carry a "confidence: LOW" qualifier in context.

